"Ordered clauses: the first matching head supplies the result."
\fact(0) = 1
\fact(n) = n*\fact(n-1)
\fact(5)
(\fact(0) = 1)

"Literal patterns and a catch-all."
f(-2) = 20
f("yes") = 30
f(\true) = 40
f(x) = 50
f(-2.)
f("yes")
f(\true)
f(1)

"Aliases and partials see later additions."
g(0,x) = x
h = g
p = g(2,·)
g(n,x) = n+x
h(2,3)
p(3)

"Each nested function captures its defining call."
k(a) = (
r(0) = a
r(n) = n+r(n-1)
r
)
s = k(10)
s(3)
